From: FlyFish-go <2541290956@qq.com>
Subject: net: ip_tunnel: check the input device before the VXLAN test

The QSDK change to iptunnel_xmit() looks up the input device from
skb->skb_iif and passes it to netif_is_vxlan() without a NULL check.
Packets the router sends itself through a UDP tunnel have no input
interface, so in_dev is NULL and netif_is_vxlan() dereferences it.
A WireGuard handshake response crashes the kernel this way:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000050c
  PC is at iptunnel_xmit+0x248/0x2a4
  ... wg_socket_send_skb_to_peer [wireguard] ...

Only test for VXLAN when there is an input device.
---
--- a/net/ipv4/ip_tunnel_core.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ip_tunnel_core.c
@@ -86,7 +86,8 @@
 		in_dev = __dev_get_by_index(&init_net, skb_iif);
 	}
 
-	if (proto == IPPROTO_IPV6 || proto == IPPROTO_GRE || netif_is_vxlan(in_dev)) {
+	if (proto == IPPROTO_IPV6 || proto == IPPROTO_GRE ||
+	    (in_dev && netif_is_vxlan(in_dev))) {
 		skb->skb_iif = skb_iif;
 	}
 
